          "footnotes": [
            "Visit detail: C = clinic; T = telehealth visit (shaded columns)",
            "Concomitant medications: Collect all data for ongoing medications at the time of consent and concomitant medications of interest (Section 6.9.1).",
            "Adverse events (AEs): Any events that occur after signing the informed consent are considered AEs as defined in Section 10.3. Additional data are collected for certain AEs. See Section 8.3.3 for AESIs.",
            "Pre-colonoscopy instructions and reminders: Includes eDiary compliance, dates, and bowel preparation/procedure.",
            "Waist circumference: See Section 10.9.",
            "Weight: See Section 10.9.",
            "Complete physical examination: The complete physical examination excludes pelvic, rectal, and breast examinations, unless clinically indicated. All remaining physical examinations throughout the study should include a symptom-directed physical evaluation, as well as an examination of the heart, lungs, abdomen, neurological system, thyroid, and visual examination of the skin. See Section 8.2.1.",
            "Symptom-directed physical assessment: Perform as indicated based on participant status and standard of care. May be performed by a qualified personnel per local regulations. Every symptom-directed examination should also include an examination of the heart, lungs, abdomen, neurological system, thyroid, and visual examination of the skin. At least every third month after screening, assess for TB risk factors, and for signs and symptoms of active TB, including an assessment of peripheral lymph nodes (Sections 8.2.1 and 8.2.10).",
            "Vital signs: Include pulse rate, blood pressure, respiratory rate, and body temperature. Measured after participant has been sitting at least 5 minutes. See Sections 8.2.2 and 10.9.",
            "Extraintestinal manifestations (EIMs): See Section 8.2.1.",
            "DXA scan, whole body: See Section 8.1.3.1. If not completed, will not be considered a protocol deviation. Participants should fast for at least 8 hours without eating or drinking (except water) before each DXA scan. No water should be consumed within 2 hours before each DXA scan. * At ED, repeat if more than 3 months have passed since the last scan.",
            "Clinician-administered assessments (paper): Collect after the assessment of AEs.",
            "Review and reinforcement of diet, exercise, and lifestyle goals: See Section 5.3.1",
            "Lifestyle counseling (diet, exercise, and lifestyle goals): See Sections 5.3.1 and 5.3.2. *The window period for these visits should be up to 14 days.",
            "Participant dosing diary (paper): Participants will maintain as study diary to document dosing information.",
            "Participant 3-day nutrition and physical activity log (paper): See Section 5.3.1.",
            "Participant daily diary (electronic): The daily eDiary includes: Rectal Bleeding (RB), Stool Frequency (SF), PGR-S, and Urgency NRS.",
            "Laboratory tests and sample collections: All laboratory tests will be performed in non-fasting state.",
            "Urine pregnancy (local): *For telehealth visits, pregnancy tests will be home pregnancy tests. For IOCBP, pregnancy test result must be available before the first dose of study intervention. Perform additional pregnancy tests if a menstrual period is missed, if there is clinical suspicion of pregnancy, or as if required by local law or regulation (Section 8.2.6).",
            "Follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH): * Optional per investigator's discretion; perform as needed to confirm postmenopausal status in individuals AFAB. See Section 8.2.6.",
            "Hepatitis B (HBV) DNA: Only for participants who are anti-HBc positive at Visit 1. See Section 8.2.11.",
            "Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR): Calculated using CKD-EPI Cystatin C Equation 2012 (NKF [WWW]).",
            "Pharmacokinetics (PK) samples (mirikizumab; pre-dose): Collect samples before the dosing, if dosing is scheduled. Collect additional samples at specified times relative to onset of hypersensitivity events (Section 10.2.1).",
            "Pharmacokinetics (PK) samples (tirzepatide; pre-dose): Collect samples before the dosing, if dosing is scheduled. Collect additional samples at specified times relative to onset of hypersensitivity events (Section 10.2.1).",
            "Immunogenicity (ADA) (anti-mirikizumab antibodies) samples (pre-dose): Collect samples before the dosing, if dosing is scheduled. Collect additional samples at specified times relative to onset of hypersensitivity events (Section 10.2.1).",
            "Immunogenicity (ADA) (anti-tirzepatide antibodies) samples (pre-dose): Collect samples before the dosing, if dosing is scheduled. Collect additional samples at specified times relative to onset of hypersensitivity events (Section 10.2.1).",
            "Micronutrient panels: * Additional micronutrient testing should be done if the PI suspects the participant is at risk having malnutrition, for example, caloric intake is significantly reduced to below 800 to 1200 kcal; a participant's BMI falls below 22 kg/m2, or in participants with T2DM, weight loss is >20% or >4 kg/month. See Sections 8.2.13, 10.2, 10.2.2, and 10.7.",
            "Dispense stool collection kit: * Dispense as needed.",
            "C. Difficile testing: Additional C. Difficile testing may be done at the investigator's discretion.",
            "Stool culture: Additional stool testing is allowed throughout the study at the investigator's discretion. *Additional local stool testing (for example, ova and parasites) is allowed at the investigator's discretion.",
            "Exploratory biomarkers (colon/rectum tissue): Obtained from the endoscopic biopsy.",
            "Colonoscopy with biopsy: Sigmoidoscopy is allowed, but colonoscopy is preferred; see Section 8.1.1.2. If the participant is not compliant with the eDiary entry (Section 8.1.1.1) within the colonoscopy visit interval, contact the Lilly medical monitor regarding rescheduling the colonoscopy. *Unscheduled sigmoidoscopy or colonoscopy per investigator's discretion (Section 6.9.6). ** No need to repeat colonoscopy if completed up to 3 months prior. Second colonoscopy is allowed if inadequate preparation or equipment issues. During colonoscopy and sigmoidoscopy biopsies will be obtained, and additional colonic/rectal biopsies will be obtained for exploratory biomarker analysis.",
            "Dispense ancillary supplies to participant: * Dispense as needed.",
            "Abbreviations: AFAB = identified female at birth; AESIs = adverse events of special interest; anti-HBc = anti-hepatitis B core antibody; BMI = body mass index; C-SSRS = Columbia-Suicide Severity Rating Scale; CKD-EPI = Chronic Kidney Disease Epidemiology Collaboration; CT = computed tomography; DXA = dual-energy x-ray absorptiometry; ECG = electrocardiogram; ED = early discontinuation; eDiary = electronic diary; ICF = informed consent form; IWRS = interactive web-response system; mMS = modified Mayo score; NRS = numeric rating scale; PI = principal investigator; PGR-S = Patient's Global Rating of Severity; SC = subcutaneous; T2DM = type 2 diabetes mellitus; TB = tuberculosis; UC = ulcerative colitis; UV = unscheduled visit.",
            "a. For participants whose visits have extended windows, additional study intervention may need to be provided to avoid study intervention interruption and maintain overall integrity of the study."
          ]
        }
